From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] client: bare_app: ODROID-GO Ultra keys, the right stick as the D-pad

The GO Ultra has a row of six F keys under the screen and a second stick.
With BARE_APP_VCMI_KEYS=ogu (set by bare_app per board) its F keys go
their own way: F1 (minimise) and F6 (quit) stay bare_app's, F2 and F3
are held as Ctrl and Shift (split one creature off, split evenly), F4
accepts, F5 ends the turn when the adventure map can, elsewhere it is
the keyboard's Escape: cancel, and back in the main menu's pages, where
the controller's cancel does nothing. Without the variable the keys stay
as on the OGA. The right stick does what the D-pad does, past half its
travel (the OGA has none).

